title: Malicious Exodus Wallet Installer - MSI Execution via Msiexec
id: a7e3b1c4-92f6-4d8a-b5e1-3c7f9a2d8e4b
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects msiexec.exe executing MSI packages from paths associated with
    the trojanized Exodus cryptocurrency wallet installer (Huntress, 2026).
    The malicious installer modifies three files in the legitimate Exodus
    package while deploying a modular RAT with VNC, SOCKS proxy, and
    browser-data theft capabilities. Attackers used JavaScript files
    masquerading as PDFs (.pdf.js) to trigger msiexec silently.
references:
    - https://cyberpress.org
    - https://gbhackers.com
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/02
tags:
    - attack.t1204
    - attack.t1059
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_msiexec:
        Image|endswith: '\msiexec.exe'
    selection_flags:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '/i '
            - '/quiet'
            - '/qn'
            - '/passive'
    selection_suspicious_path:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '\Users\Public\'
            - '\ProgramData\'
            - '\AppData\Local\Temp\'
            - '\Downloads\'
    condition: selection_msiexec and selection_flags and selection_suspicious_path
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate software installations using msiexec from temp directories
level: medium
